{
  "name": "Archive and log invoices from Gmail with SFTP and Google Sheets — V2 — Revised",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Archive and log invoice PDFs\n\n### How it works\n1. A manual run or six-hour schedule retrieves matching Gmail messages, including read emails.\n2. Each PDF attachment is separated and its text is extracted.\n3. Configurable rules validate the provider, invoice number, date and total, then build a canonical filename.\n4. Four provider branches upload PDFs over SFTP and upsert the invoice register in Google Sheets. Source emails are retained.\n\n### Setup\n- [ ] Connect Gmail OAuth2 and narrow the email query to your invoice senders.\n- [ ] Customize the rules in **Parse Invoice Details** using text from real invoices.\n- [ ] Create the four `/invoices/` category folders and connect all SFTP nodes.\n- [ ] Share your spreadsheet with the Google service account. Replace the spreadsheet ID in all four Sheets nodes.\n- [ ] Create the `Invoices` tab with Provider, Category, Invoice Number, Date, Amount, File and Unique Key columns.\n- [ ] Test every provider and a multi-PDF email before enabling the schedule.\n\n### Customization\nAdapt provider rules and destination folders. Image-only PDFs require OCR. Repeated runs upload the same filename and upsert the same key; confirm your SFTP overwrite behavior.",
        "height": 544,
        "width": 640
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -816,
        -80
      ],
      "id": "9e625e5b-d30f-4472-9b4e-5664156d0325",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
